## Phases A–D — Stabilization & standardization (added work)

These items were **not** in the original Q&A but are now part of the platform.

### Phase A — Single source of truth (Integrity)

- **`apps/configs/default_system_settings.py`** and **`app_definitions.py`**: canonical metadata for all V1 apps
- Each Django app calls `AppRegistry().register_from_definition('<name>')` on startup
- `POST /api/v1/config/registered-apps/sync_registry/` reconciles DB with definitions (replaces broken `register_v1_apps` data)
- `python manage.py register_all_apps` uses the same definitions
- `RegisteredAppManager` wired on the model (`.critical()`, `.by_priority()`, etc.)
- Health probe URLs resolved via `CONFIG_INTERNAL_HEALTH_BASE_URL`

### Phase B — App Registry UI (Availability + Integrity)

- Route: **`/config/registry`**
- Registered apps table with CIA badges, RPO/RTO, retention, dependency count
- Recovery sequence and priority order views
- Dependency editor (Super Admin)
- Edit modal for display name, criticality, priority, health endpoint

### Phase C — Real-time (real-change)

- **`ConfigProgressBroadcaster`**: `group_send` for backup, DR, and maintenance events
- WebSocket consumers: backup job, DR execution, maintenance status
- Frontend: fixed `maintenance_{tenantId}` socket IDs; removed duplicate `WebSocketProvider` / dead Redux WS middleware
- **`GlobalMaintenanceBanner`** in main application layout
- Live indicators on backup/DR progress components

### Phase D — Persisted system settings (real-change)

- Model: **`ConfigSystemSettings`** (singleton JSON + version)
- API: `GET/PATCH /api/v1/config/system-settings/`, `POST .../reset/`
- Frontend: all settings tabs load/save via API; **Save All**, per-tab save, **Reset Defaults**
- Settings drive: health failure thresholds, maintenance overlap blocking, notification alert thresholds
- Migration: `0003_config_system_settings`; seed: `python manage.py seed_config_settings`

