## Conclusion

The Falcon PMS Config system **delivers the core promise** of the original training material: protected data through backups, planned maintenance, health-aware automation, disaster recovery with drills, and administrative visibility through audit and dashboards.

**Fully delivered in this implementation cycle:** standardized app registry, CIA-oriented controls, App Registry UI, WebSocket progress, global maintenance banner, and **persisted system settings** replacing stub “Save All” behavior.

**Still aspirational or process-only:** blackout calendars, custom health UI, record-level restore UX, SMS, and some narrative defaults (schedule times, tiered retention marketing copy) should be aligned with what is configured in each deployment.

For operators, the practical rule unchanged: **test backups and DR drills before an emergency**. The product now provides the registry, APIs, UI, and real-time feedback to make that testing straightforward.

